`# Stage 2: Visualizations to Reinforce Stage1 Insights

## 1. Regional Conversion Rate Trends

![Conversion Rate Trends by Region](./regional_conversion_trends.png)

*Caption:* Daily average store listing conversion rate across four major regions from April to October 2024, showing effectively flat trends with no statistically significant decay or improvement. This aligns with the Stage1 finding that acquisition cost-efficiency remained stable across all regions.

## 2. Device-Level Install Intensity Trends

![Device-Level Install Intensity Trends](./device_install_intensity_trends.png)

*Caption:* 7‑day moving average of install intensity (installs per active device) for twelve popular device models. All series exhibit near‑zero slopes, confirming Stage1’s conclusion that acquisition efficiency does not meaningfully decay or grow on any device type.

## 3. Non‑Linear Relationship: Conversion Rate vs. Quality Score & Crash Rate

![Conversion vs Quality Score](./conversion_vs_quality.png)

*Caption:* Quadratic fits between daily conversion rate (per app) and quality score for each of the eight apps. All R² values are below 0.02, meaning quality score explains less than 2% of conversion‑rate variation.

![Conversion vs Crash Rate](./conversion_vs_crash.png)

*Caption:* Quadratic fits between daily conversion rate (per app) and crash rate per 1k sessions, likewise showing R² < 0.02. This lack of explanatory power confirms Stage1’s insight that store‑listing conversion is driven by factors other than the measured technical‑quality metrics.

## 4. Revenue per Active Device vs. Active Devices by Market Maturity

![Revenue vs Active Devices Low Maturity](./revenue_vs_active_low_maturity.png)

*Caption:* In low‑maturity periods (below‑median cumulative installs), revenue per active device exhibits a moderate negative correlation with the number of active devices, supporting the Stage1 finding that scaling the user base in early growth phases tends to dilute per‑device revenue.

![Revenue vs Active Devices High Maturity](./revenue_vs_active_high_maturity.png)

*Caption:* In high‑maturity periods (above‑median cumulative installs), the correlation disappears. This validates Stage1’s recommendation to focus on cost efficiency and up‑selling rather than expecting revenue per device to improve with further scale.

## 5. Interaction Effect of App Update Frequency

![Update Frequency vs Active Devices](./update_vs_active_devices.png)

*Caption:* Scatter plot of 7‑day moving average of daily update events against active devices (last 30 days) for all apps, colored by package. The near‑zero overall correlation (+0.009) matches Stage1’s conclusion that update frequency has no meaningful impact on active‑device counts.

![Update Frequency vs Rolling Average Rating](./update_vs_rating.png)

*Caption:* Scatter plot of update frequency versus rolling 30‑day average rating, again showing a very weak positive association (correlation +0.039). While updates may slightly improve satisfaction, the effect is too small to drive strategy.

---
*Visualizations created from the dacomp‑070 dataset (April–October 2024).*`)
