Our earlier composite (equal-ish weights) gave accuracy 74.3% for baseline (duration+frequency). The correlation-weighted composite gave 95.2% accuracy on that same "ground truth". However that seems biased. Let's test with a different ground truth: define high-value as those in top 30% of sum_minutes and top 30% of avg_nps_rating and top 30% of count_feature_clicking_visitors (maybe stringent). Then we compute baseline vs correlation-weighted.

