Maybe we can compute retention by using active_retention_rate_week from persons, but we need to attribute each person to campaigns they received. Since we don't have that mapping, we might need to assume that retention metrics are aggregated at the person level across all campaigns, which is not useful.

Given the time, I'll focus on open and click rates and also compute a derived metric "conversion rate" = count_placed_order / count_received_email as a proxy for campaign effectiveness. Then we can see how timing and subject affect conversion.

Also, we need to control for audience size and de-noising. We'll filter out campaigns where count_received_email is anomalous (e.g., outliers using IQR). Also perhaps filter where total_count_unique_people is too small.

